1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,140
Good morning. The alarm went off a few minutes ago,

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:07,520
and if you are honest, your first thought was probably not thank you.

3
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:10,660
It was closer to: Already? Another day.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,640
Another list. The same worries you carried to bed last night,

5
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:17,580
waiting for you before your feet even touched the floor.

6
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:21,540
You know in your head that a new morning is a gift.

7
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:26,260
Your heart just feels flat, and gratitude sounds like a word other people

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:27,880
say more easily than you do.

9
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:29,680
Stay here for a moment.

10
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:32,160
You do not have to manufacture a feeling.

11
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:35,160
You only have to be honest in front of a God who is

12
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,600
already awake, already near, already looking at you with kindness.

13
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:44,060
Because something is true about this specific morning that has nothing to do

14
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:48,320
with your mood. God's mercy did not run out overnight.

15
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:52,500
His compassion arrived fresh with the light, and this day is not a

16
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:56,120
copy of yesterday. It is new, and so is he toward you.

17
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,040
So let it be simple.

18
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:02,540
Breathe once, slowly. Let your shoulders come down.

19
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,160
In the next few minutes we will thank God together,

20
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:07,940
tell him the truth, put down what we have been carrying,

21
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:12,620
ask him for what we actually need, and walk into this day steady instead of rushed.

22
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:15,840
If you want to keep beginning your mornings in his presence,

23
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:18,520
subscribe and pray with us each day.

24
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:23,360
Now, wherever you are, let us come to our Father together.

25
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:30,780
Heavenly Father, good morning. Before I ask you for one single thing,

26
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:34,900
I want to stop and thank you, because you were here long before

27
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:36,100
I opened my eyes.

28
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,440
While the room was still dark and the house was still quiet,

29
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:44,760
you were keeping watch. You held my breathing steady while I was not thinking about it.

30
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:47,820
You kept my heart beating while I was too asleep to be grateful.

31
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:51,560
Thank you for a love that keeps working when I am not awake to notice it.

32
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,480
Thank you that you are not a distant God I have to reach

33
00:01:54,520 --> 00:01:58,180
with the right words. You are near, and you are kind.

34
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:01,580
You are patient with me in a way I have not always been

35
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:05,540
patient with myself. You do not sigh when you see me coming.

36
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:09,400
You do not read back the list of mornings I forgot you.

37
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,780
You welcome me, and you have never once been too busy for the

38
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:13,900
sound of my voice.

39
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:17,320
I praise you today for who you are, not only for what you

40
00:02:17,360 --> 00:02:22,280
give. You are faithful, and that is not a poetic word.

41
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:26,640
It means you have never failed me, not in the seasons I understood,

42
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:29,160
and not in the ones I still do not.

43
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:33,320
You are good when the news is easy and when the news is

44
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:38,240
heavy. You are wise when your answers arrive quickly and when they take years.

45
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:43,680
You are strong in ways I have quietly leaned on without ever saying thank you.

46
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:48,340
Lord, you are the source of every good thing in my life.

47
00:02:48,820 --> 00:02:52,560
Every ability I have was placed in me by you.

48
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:56,380
Every person who has truly loved me was sent by you.

49
00:02:56,480 --> 00:03:00,060
Every door I walked through, every danger I never knew I passed,

50
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:03,980
every quiet rescue I never saw happen, came from your hand.

51
00:03:04,160 --> 00:03:06,760
I did not build this life on my own.

52
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,820
You have been holding it.

53
00:03:08,900 --> 00:03:11,560
And thank you for the years I did not thank you.

54
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,900
The seasons when I was too young to notice,

55
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:17,480
too busy to look up, or too angry to speak to you.

56
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,860
You kept giving anyway.

57
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:23,280
You gave sunrises to a person who did not acknowledge them,

58
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:26,180
food to a person who forgot to bless it,

59
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:28,900
and grace to a person who called it luck.

60
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:32,560
That is not a small kindness, Father.

61
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:36,860
That is the character of a God who loves before he is loved back.

62
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:42,340
So this morning I lift my heart before I lift anything else. I worship you.

63
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:45,660
You are the God who spoke light into the darkness at the beginning,

64
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:49,680
and you are the same God speaking peace into me right now.

65
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:52,040
You do not need my praise to be great,

66
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:56,460
and still you receive it, because you are a Father who delights in his children.

67
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,860
Let this be the first sound of my day.

68
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:04,285
Not complaint. Not calculation. Just gratitude, honest and unhurried,

69
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:06,490
offered to the one who deserves it.

70
00:04:06,530 --> 00:04:08,030
Come into this morning, Lord.

71
00:04:08,170 --> 00:04:11,610
Fill this room, this quiet, this heart of mine.

72
00:04:11,990 --> 00:04:16,190
Before anything else happens, let me remember that I belong to you,

73
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:21,050
and that being yours is already more than I could earn. Thank you, Father.

74
00:04:23,650 --> 00:04:26,690
Thank you for being exactly who you say you are.

75
00:04:27,790 --> 00:04:31,310
Lord, your word tells me why this morning is different,

76
00:04:33,010 --> 00:04:34,930
and I want to hold on to it.

77
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:40,730
In Lamentations chapter three, verses twenty-two and twenty-three, you say that

78
00:04:40,770 --> 00:04:43,750
because of your great love we are not consumed,

79
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:46,430
for your compassions never fail.

80
00:04:46,890 --> 00:04:47,990
They are new every morning;

81
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:49,570
great is your faithfulness.

82
00:04:50,410 --> 00:04:53,610
Father, I remember who wrote those words.

83
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:56,450
They were written by a man surrounded by ruins,

84
00:04:56,750 --> 00:05:00,230
looking at a city that had fallen, grieving losses that were not going

85
00:05:00,270 --> 00:05:01,710
to be undone that week.

86
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:04,210
He was not writing from a comfortable place.

87
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:06,350
He was writing in the middle of the wreckage,

88
00:05:06,690 --> 00:05:10,390
and there in the ashes he found one thing still standing.

89
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:13,530
Your mercy showed up again in the morning.

90
00:05:13,870 --> 00:05:15,990
That is why I can trust this verse.

91
00:05:16,290 --> 00:05:19,210
It was not written by someone whose life was easy.

92
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:22,690
It was written by someone who had nothing left except you,

93
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:25,490
and discovered that you were enough to start again.

94
00:05:25,590 --> 00:05:28,770
So when I look at my own unfinished places today,

95
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:30,990
I will not pretend they are fixed.

96
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:32,570
I will do what he did.

97
00:05:32,810 --> 00:05:35,630
I will look for the mercy that arrived with the light.

98
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:37,630
It came without me asking.

99
00:05:37,910 --> 00:05:39,830
It came before I proved anything.

100
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:44,030
It came while I was still asleep and still failing and still unsure.

101
00:05:44,330 --> 00:05:46,090
That is what mercy means.

102
00:05:46,330 --> 00:05:48,570
It is not a reward for a good week.

103
00:05:48,690 --> 00:05:52,490
It is the kindness of God meeting me at the beginning of a new one.

104
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:55,550
And it is measured out for one day only,

105
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:57,490
which is exactly what I need.

106
00:05:57,730 --> 00:06:01,210
You did not hand me enough mercy for the whole year at once,

107
00:06:01,310 --> 00:06:05,210
because I would try to manage it the way I manage everything else.

108
00:06:05,410 --> 00:06:09,370
You give it fresh, morning by morning, so that I keep coming back

109
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:11,890
to you instead of leaning on my own supply.

110
00:06:12,050 --> 00:06:16,000
So I am here again, holding out my hands for today's portion,

111
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,260
and it is enough.

112
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:21,280
Your word also says, in Psalm chapter one hundred eighteen,

113
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:25,700
verse twenty-four, that the Lord has done it this very day;

114
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:28,360
let us rejoice today and be glad.

115
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:32,560
Not some better day. Not the day when everything is finally settled.

116
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:36,200
This one. The Thursday with the crowded schedule.

117
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:40,100
The morning with the tired body and the ordinary sky.

118
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:42,880
You made it, and you made it on purpose,

119
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:45,200
and you placed me inside it awake.

120
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:50,260
Lord, teach me to read my life the way your word reads it.

121
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,520
Not by what is missing, but by what is being given.

122
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:57,400
Not by yesterday's ending, but by this morning's beginning.

123
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:02,520
Let this truth sink deeper than my feelings, so that when the day

124
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:05,760
pushes back, I still know what is underneath me.

125
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,800
Your compassion has not failed.

126
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:09,380
It has not thinned out.

127
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:13,720
It is new, and it is here, and it is for me today.

128
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:18,880
Father, if your mercy is new this morning, then this is the safest

129
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,560
place to be honest with you.

130
00:07:20,660 --> 00:07:23,560
So let me stop performing and simply talk.

131
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,280
I have not been grateful.

132
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,780
I have been busy.

133
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:32,760
I have looked at a life full of your kindness and still found

134
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:35,820
something to complain about before I even left the kitchen.

135
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:40,460
I have measured my day against someone else's and let comparison steal the

136
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:44,420
joy of what you already placed in my hands. Forgive me, Lord.

137
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:46,840
Not with shame, but with cleansing.

138
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:51,060
You are faithful and just to forgive when I come to you honestly.

139
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:53,240
I confess the hurry, too.

140
00:07:53,540 --> 00:07:58,620
I have treated my mornings as something to survive instead of something to receive.

141
00:07:58,900 --> 00:08:01,800
I have handed the first and the best of my attention to a

142
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:05,300
screen and given you what was left over when I was already tired.

143
00:08:05,660 --> 00:08:08,980
I have prayed while walking out the door and called it devotion.

144
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,800
Meet me here in the truth of that and change the pattern in

145
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:15,140
me, gently, day by day.

146
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:18,340
And forgive me for how easily I take people for granted.

147
00:08:18,640 --> 00:08:22,740
I have walked past the ones who love me most without really seeing them.

148
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:30,260
I have answered someone at home while my mind was somewhere else entirely.

149
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:33,980
I have said I am fine when I meant I am tired,

150
00:08:34,020 --> 00:08:37,200
and said nothing when I meant help me.

151
00:08:37,242 --> 00:08:38,480
Soften that in me today.

152
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:43,360
Let the people closest to me feel wanted, not merely tolerated by someone

153
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:44,740
who is always in a hurry.

154
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:49,000
And Lord, I put down what I have been carrying since yesterday.

155
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:51,940
The conversation that ended badly.

156
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,840
The mistake I keep replaying at two in the morning.

157
00:08:55,620 --> 00:09:00,340
The resentment I have been feeding quietly because it felt easier than forgiveness.

158
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:05,220
The worry that pretends to be responsibility but has never solved a single thing.

159
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:08,240
I am not going to carry these into today as if you were

160
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,480
unable to hold them.

161
00:09:09,800 --> 00:09:12,600
I open my hands, one thing at a time.

162
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:15,800
The bills I do not know how to cover this month.

163
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:20,000
The person whose silence hurts more than an argument would.

164
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:23,740
The decision I keep pushing to next week because I am afraid of

165
00:09:23,780 --> 00:09:28,420
getting it wrong. The fear about my health, my family, my future.

166
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,400
I lay them here in front of you.

167
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:34,200
If they belong back in my hands later, put them there yourself,

168
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:36,440
and give me the strength to hold them well.

169
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:41,960
Cleanse my heart of the bitterness that hardens me and the self-pity that isolates me.

170
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:45,600
Where I have wronged someone, give me the humility to go and repair

171
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:48,000
it, even if it costs my pride.

172
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:51,880
Where I have been wounded, take the blade out of my hands so

173
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,120
I am not carrying it into my home or my work today.

174
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:57,120
Make me light again, Father.

175
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:03,140
Not careless, but unburdened. I would rather walk into this day empty-handed with

176
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:05,560
you than fully loaded and alone.

177
00:10:06,860 --> 00:10:11,280
Thank you, Lord, for the mercies I stopped noticing a long time ago.

178
00:10:12,100 --> 00:10:17,040
Now that my hands are open, let me actually see what is already in them.

179
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:20,100
Thank you for a bed to wake up in and a roof that

180
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:21,260
held through the night.

181
00:10:21,780 --> 00:10:25,120
Thank you for water that runs warm when I turn the tap,

182
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:28,380
and for the ordinary miracle of clean water at all,

183
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,780
which so much of the world still waits for.

184
00:10:30,980 --> 00:10:34,120
Thank you for clothes that fit, for shoes by the door,

185
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:37,120
for something in the kitchen to eat before I go.

186
00:10:37,420 --> 00:10:39,140
These are not small things.

187
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:42,880
They are daily answers to prayers I never remembered to pray.

188
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:47,500
Thank you for this body, even the parts that ache.

189
00:10:48,320 --> 00:10:51,560
Thank you for legs that carry me, hands that work,

190
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:54,560
eyes that see the light coming through the window.

191
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:58,660
Thank you for a mind that can think and remember and hope.

192
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,500
If I am moving slower than I used to,

193
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:03,540
thank you that I am still moving.

194
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:08,260
If I am tired, thank you that the tiredness came from a life

195
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:09,460
with something in it.

196
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,800
Thank you for the people breathing under this same roof,

197
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:16,680
or in another city, or in a voice message waiting for me.

198
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:19,640
Thank you for whoever is still asleep in the next room.

199
00:11:19,820 --> 00:11:23,040
Thank you for the friend who checks on me without being asked.

200
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:27,860
Thank you for the family members who love me imperfectly and stay anyway.

201
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:32,480
Cover each of them today with your protection and your peace,

202
00:11:32,520 --> 00:11:36,510
and let them feel, somehow, that they are prayed for.

203
00:11:36,550 --> 00:11:39,740
Father, open my eyes wider than my worries.

204
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:44,840
Let me notice the first cup of coffee in my hands and remember it was provided.

205
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:49,160
Let me notice a neighbor's greeting and see your kindness in it.

206
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:53,340
Let me notice the sound of rain, the taste of bread,

207
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:57,700
the fact that my name is known and loved by the God who made the stars.

208
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:00,840
And give me a memory that works in the right direction.

209
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:03,540
I remember my losses so easily.

210
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:07,000
Help me to remember your rescues just as clearly.

211
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:09,120
The month that somehow got covered.

212
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,440
The wrong turn that protected me.

213
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:14,200
The friendship that arrived exactly when I was alone.

214
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:17,780
The strength that showed up on the day I truly did not have any.

215
00:12:17,960 --> 00:12:21,180
Thank you also for the ordinary days I never think to mention.

216
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,180
The Tuesdays when nothing broke.

217
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:25,780
The nights when no one in this house was in danger.

218
00:12:26,700 --> 00:12:30,440
The month the car kept running, the year my body held up,

219
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:33,800
the long season when nothing dramatic happened at all.

220
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:39,660
I have prayed hardest in emergencies, Lord, but you have carried me most

221
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,940
often in the quiet stretches.

222
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:45,700
Thank you for the plain, unremarkable mercies.

223
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:48,020
They were you, all along.

224
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,940
Every good thing in my life came down from you,

225
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:55,600
Father. Nothing here is an accident, and nothing here is owed to me.

226
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:59,820
Thank you for a life that is fuller than my complaints have admitted.

227
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,100
Lord, in a few minutes this quiet will end.

228
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:08,600
The door will open, the messages will start, and the day will begin

229
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:10,360
asking things of me.

230
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:14,480
So I am praying now for the version of me that walks out of this room.

231
00:13:15,240 --> 00:13:19,300
In Psalm chapter five, verse three, your word says,

232
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:22,240
in the morning, Lord, you hear my voice.

233
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:27,120
In the morning I lay my requests before you and wait expectantly.

234
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:29,100
That is what I am doing.

235
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,880
I am not just talking to myself before work.

236
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:34,780
I am bringing my requests to a Father who hears,

237
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:38,240
and then I am going out to watch for your hand in the hours ahead.

238
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:40,820
So bless the ordinary work of this day.

239
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:44,660
Whether I am opening an inbox, standing in a classroom,

240
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:50,500
driving a route, serving behind a counter, sitting through a meeting I did not choose,

241
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:54,400
or caring for a child or a parent who cannot care for themselves,

242
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:56,720
let me do it as work offered to you.

243
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:01,740
Give me diligence when the task is dull and integrity when no one

244
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:07,000
is watching. Let excellence be my quiet way of saying thank you.

245
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:10,909
And give me one real pause somewhere in the middle of this day.

246
00:14:10,949 --> 00:14:13,080
Not a longer break, just a moment.

247
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:16,360
When I sit down to eat, or wait at a light,

248
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:18,980
or stand in a line I did not plan for,

249
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:23,020
let me use those seconds to look up instead of reaching for something to scroll.

250
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:25,960
Meet me there the way you are meeting me now.

251
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:28,760
I do not want to speak with you at sunrise and then run

252
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:30,860
the rest of the day on my own strength.

253
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:36,300
Protect my gratitude when the pressure arrives, Father, because I know how quickly

254
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:43,100
it leaks. The moment something goes wrong, my heart forgets everything that has gone right.

255
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:46,420
So when the plan changes, when the message is sharp,

256
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:50,300
when the traffic stops, when the day gets longer than I planned,

257
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:53,680
remind me of one thing I can thank you for right then.

258
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:56,740
One thing is enough to turn my heart back around.

259
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:02,280
Guard my mouth today. Let me not sharpen my tiredness into words that

260
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,260
wound the people closest to me.

261
00:15:04,460 --> 00:15:07,080
Give me patience with the coworker who tests it,

262
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:10,360
gentleness with the family member who repeats the same story,

263
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:14,060
kindness with the stranger who is having a worse morning than mine.

264
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:19,000
Where I have influence, let me use it to lift and not to press down.

265
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:22,060
Give me wisdom in the decisions I must make.

266
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:26,300
Show me what to say yes to and what to release without guilt.

267
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:30,660
Slow me down before I answer in anger, and steady me before I

268
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:33,300
sign, promise, or send.

269
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,600
Let your Spirit be the voice I recognize first,

270
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:39,340
above the noise, above my own fear.

271
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:44,300
And Lord, let someone be better off for having crossed my path today.

272
00:15:44,980 --> 00:15:48,560
A word of encouragement. A small act of help.

273
00:15:49,140 --> 00:15:50,800
A moment of real attention.

274
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:54,360
Let the gratitude you are building in me spill over into the way

275
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:58,920
I treat people, so that this prayer does not end at the door.

276
00:15:59,420 --> 00:16:02,220
Father, there are things in my life that still do not have an

277
00:16:02,260 --> 00:16:05,680
answer, and I want to be honest about them rather than skip past

278
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,300
them with a cheerful voice.

279
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,660
There is a result I am still waiting for.

280
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,020
A door that has not opened.

281
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,980
A person who has not come home.

282
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:19,660
A number in an account that does not stretch far enough.

283
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:23,200
A prayer I have prayed so many times that I have started to

284
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:27,540
say it quietly, almost carefully, as though I do not want to ask again.

285
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:32,430
Your word says, in First Thessalonians chapter five, verse eighteen,

286
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:38,920
to give thanks in all circumstances, for this is God's will for you in Christ Jesus.

287
00:16:39,260 --> 00:16:41,660
Not thanks for all circumstances.

288
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:49,640
I do not have to call the hard thing good.

289
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:52,980
But in it, even here, I can thank you,

290
00:16:53,020 --> 00:16:56,100
because you are in this waiting with me and you have not been

291
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:58,440
careless with a single day of it.

292
00:16:59,220 --> 00:17:02,140
So I thank you for what I know while I wait for what I do not.

293
00:17:02,420 --> 00:17:05,180
I thank you that you hear me, that you are not delayed by

294
00:17:05,220 --> 00:17:08,700
confusion, that nothing about my situation is unknown to you.

295
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:11,940
I thank you that my life is not being run by chance.

296
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:13,360
You see the whole picture.

297
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:18,060
I only see this morning, and this morning I choose to trust the

298
00:17:18,100 --> 00:17:19,820
character of the one who sees the rest.

299
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:22,560
I will not tell you how to answer, Father.

300
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:24,360
I will not demand a date.

301
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:27,920
I will ask honestly, and then I will leave it with you.

302
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:30,340
Provide what my family needs.

303
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,920
Bring healing where there is sickness.

304
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,780
Restore what has been broken.

305
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:39,660
Open the way that is right for me and close the ones that

306
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:43,540
would harm me, even if closing them disappoints me at first.

307
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:46,560
And while I wait, do something in me.

308
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:49,860
Let this season make me deeper instead of harder.

309
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:53,220
Teach me the patience I have avoided learning.

310
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,540
Take out the pride that only wants your gifts,

311
00:17:55,580 --> 00:17:58,040
and leave a heart that wants you.

312
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:01,540
If the waiting is where I finally learn to lean on you,

313
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:04,960
then it has not been wasted, even though it has hurt.

314
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:08,640
And Lord, I am not asking for a sign in the sky.

315
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,300
I am asking for something smaller and more honest.

316
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,420
Let me know you are close today.

317
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,520
One moment of unmistakable peace.

318
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:19,400
One word from someone that lands like it came from you.

319
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:24,220
One reminder that I have not been left to figure my life out alone.

320
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:29,140
That would be enough to keep me walking, even if nothing about my

321
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:31,270
circumstances changes by tonight.

322
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,680
Keep my hope from becoming brittle.

323
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:36,440
Keep my faith honest, not loud.

324
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:40,700
And keep my eyes on you, because you have never once been unfaithful

325
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:45,580
in my life, and I have no reason to believe today is the day you start.

326
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:50,220
Lord, I am not the only one awake this morning with a heavy

327
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:53,780
heart, and gratitude was never meant to be kept for myself.

328
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:57,820
So I lift up the others who are listening, wherever they are.

329
00:18:58,100 --> 00:19:00,820
For the one who worked the night shift and is praying with tired

330
00:19:00,860 --> 00:19:05,160
eyes before finally lying down, thank you for their faithfulness.

331
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:09,880
Give them real rest and provide for the family they are working for.

332
00:19:10,260 --> 00:19:12,820
For the one waking up to an empty side of the bed,

333
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:17,280
whose grief still arrives every morning before they are ready for it, come close.

334
00:19:17,580 --> 00:19:19,480
You are near to the brokenhearted.

335
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:24,000
Sit with them in the silence and be the comfort no words have managed to be.

336
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:28,040
For the single parent already making breakfast while worrying about the end of

337
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:31,440
the month, give strength for today and unexpected help.

338
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:35,520
Let their children feel safe and loved, and let them know their quiet

339
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:37,580
sacrifices are seen by you.

340
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:41,040
For the one who dreads this specific day, the appointment,

341
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:45,620
the court date, the exam, the conversation they cannot avoid,

342
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:49,970
go before them into that room. Steady their hands.

343
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:53,110
Give them clear words and a calm heart.

344
00:19:53,410 --> 00:19:57,350
For those in hospital rooms, and for the families waiting in corridors,

345
00:19:57,950 --> 00:20:00,730
be present in a way that is unmistakable.

346
00:20:01,250 --> 00:20:03,870
Guide the doctors and nurses caring for them.

347
00:20:03,910 --> 00:20:08,210
Give comfort through the night hours and hope in the morning ones.

348
00:20:08,430 --> 00:20:11,690
For the person who has stopped praying because they felt unheard,

349
00:20:11,990 --> 00:20:15,310
and for the one who feels far from you after a season of

350
00:20:15,350 --> 00:20:18,370
wandering, thank you that you have not moved.

351
00:20:18,710 --> 00:20:23,450
Let them hear, even through this prayer, that they are still wanted at your table.

352
00:20:24,050 --> 00:20:27,750
And Father, bless the ones I would not normally think of.

353
00:20:28,110 --> 00:20:31,170
My neighbors. The people I pass without noticing.

354
00:20:32,010 --> 00:20:34,950
The ones who are hard to love, including the ones who have hurt

355
00:20:34,990 --> 00:20:36,890
me. Do good to them.

356
00:20:37,030 --> 00:20:40,550
Let mercy be my instinct instead of my last resort.

357
00:20:40,710 --> 00:20:43,850
And be with the one praying this quietly so that nobody else in

358
00:20:43,890 --> 00:20:45,210
the house can hear them.

359
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:49,170
The one in a hospital chair, in a rented room far from family,

360
00:20:49,590 --> 00:20:52,530
in a country where their own language is rarely spoken.

361
00:20:53,050 --> 00:20:55,010
They may feel unseen this morning.

362
00:20:55,270 --> 00:20:58,670
You know their name, their street, their exact situation,

363
00:20:58,850 --> 00:21:01,030
and the one thing they have not told anyone.

364
00:21:01,370 --> 00:21:02,540
Let them feel found.

365
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:05,810
Make me part of the answer where I can be.

366
00:21:06,450 --> 00:21:09,410
If someone near me needs help I am able to give,

367
00:21:09,890 --> 00:21:12,530
let me see it and not walk past it.

368
00:21:13,150 --> 00:21:16,270
Let my hands be useful, my time be shareable,

369
00:21:16,470 --> 00:21:20,730
and my gratitude be visible enough to warm somebody else's morning.

370
00:21:22,130 --> 00:21:25,670
So Father, before I stand up, let me answer you,

371
00:21:25,710 --> 00:21:28,450
because a prayer like this deserves more than a feeling.

372
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:30,010
It deserves a decision.

373
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:33,870
I choose to thank you before I see anything change.

374
00:21:34,170 --> 00:21:37,330
Not because I am strong, but because you are faithful,

375
00:21:37,590 --> 00:21:40,990
and my thanks is a response to who you already are.

376
00:21:41,310 --> 00:21:45,510
I choose gratitude as my first language today.

377
00:21:45,970 --> 00:21:50,210
Before I check anything, my first words will be thank you.

378
00:21:50,290 --> 00:21:54,090
When my mind reaches for what is wrong, I will name one thing

379
00:21:54,130 --> 00:21:57,370
that is right. When I am tempted to rehearse a complaint,

380
00:21:57,410 --> 00:22:00,330
I will rehearse your faithfulness instead.

381
00:22:01,350 --> 00:22:03,750
I will trust you with what I cannot control.

382
00:22:04,430 --> 00:22:10,150
My family's safety, this month's provision, the outcome I have been waiting for,

383
00:22:10,670 --> 00:22:12,350
the future I cannot see.

384
00:22:12,630 --> 00:22:16,030
I hand them over knowingly, and if worry picks them back up during

385
00:22:16,070 --> 00:22:20,350
the day, I will bring them here again as many times as I need to.

386
00:22:20,470 --> 00:22:22,650
I will walk into this day expecting you.

387
00:22:22,690 --> 00:22:26,090
Not expecting perfection. Expecting your presence.

388
00:22:26,710 --> 00:22:29,270
I will look for you in the meeting, in the traffic,

389
00:22:29,550 --> 00:22:33,570
in the kitchen, in the ordinary hour when nothing seems to be happening,

390
00:22:34,050 --> 00:22:36,790
believing you are working even where I cannot trace it.

391
00:22:36,830 --> 00:22:41,290
And I will let this gratitude leave my mouth and reach someone else.

392
00:22:42,010 --> 00:22:45,570
Today I will tell one person that I am thankful for them,

393
00:22:45,610 --> 00:22:47,530
and I will not wait for a better moment.

394
00:22:47,790 --> 00:22:49,010
I will send the message.

395
00:22:49,290 --> 00:22:50,510
I will say it plainly.

396
00:22:51,110 --> 00:22:54,350
Thankfulness that stays private grows cold.

397
00:22:54,550 --> 00:22:57,730
And when this day gets loud, I will come back to this.

398
00:22:57,830 --> 00:23:02,030
Not with a longer prayer, just three words. Thank you, Lord.

399
00:23:02,790 --> 00:23:05,470
I can say that in a stairwell, in a car,

400
00:23:05,670 --> 00:23:09,290
in the middle of a hard conversation, and it will still be true.

401
00:23:09,470 --> 00:23:13,670
Lord, I am not promising to feel this way all day. Feelings move.

402
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:16,670
But I am making a decision now, in the quiet,

403
00:23:16,710 --> 00:23:20,370
while my heart is soft, so that I have something to stand on

404
00:23:20,410 --> 00:23:21,670
when the noise starts.

405
00:23:22,070 --> 00:23:26,410
Whatever this day holds, I have already settled the most important thing.

406
00:23:27,170 --> 00:23:31,370
You are good, you are with me, and you are worth trusting.

407
00:23:31,730 --> 00:23:36,690
So take my willingness, small as it is, and make something faithful out

408
00:23:36,730 --> 00:23:39,150
of it. I am yours today, Father.

409
00:23:39,490 --> 00:23:43,070
Wherever you lead, I will go with a grateful heart.

410
00:23:44,290 --> 00:23:47,470
Heavenly Father, this morning started with a tired thought,

411
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:49,430
and you have turned it into thank you.

412
00:23:49,470 --> 00:23:51,750
That is your work, not mine.

413
00:23:52,050 --> 00:23:55,390
I came in flat and honest, and you met me with mercy that

414
00:23:55,430 --> 00:23:57,790
was already new before I asked for it.

415
00:23:57,830 --> 00:24:00,370
So I receive this day now as a gift,

416
00:24:00,710 --> 00:24:06,210
not a burden. I receive your compassion, fresh for these twenty-four hours.

417
00:24:06,490 --> 00:24:09,630
I receive your peace for the parts I cannot solve,

418
00:24:09,870 --> 00:24:13,310
and your strength for the parts I must simply do.

419
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:18,930
Whatever comes, I will not face it alone, and I will not face it unloved.

420
00:24:19,190 --> 00:24:22,470
Now, Father, bless the one praying this prayer.

421
00:24:22,710 --> 00:24:25,890
May your mercy meet them at the start of every morning for the

422
00:24:25,930 --> 00:24:27,090
rest of their life.

423
00:24:27,890 --> 00:24:31,550
May their eyes be opened to the good you have already placed around them.

424
00:24:31,590 --> 00:24:35,970
May gratitude become the most natural sound in their home,

425
00:24:36,010 --> 00:24:39,770
and may your peace hold steady in them all through this day.

426
00:24:40,010 --> 00:24:44,230
In the name of Jesus Christ our Lord, I pray. Amen.

427
00:24:45,850 --> 00:24:48,950
Before you go, do one small thing with me.

428
00:24:49,330 --> 00:24:52,930
Type the word grateful in the comments, as your own way of saying

429
00:24:52,970 --> 00:24:55,150
thank you to God for this new day.

430
00:24:55,570 --> 00:25:00,590
Read a few of the other comments too, and pray for one name you find there.

431
00:25:01,090 --> 00:25:04,250
If this prayer met you this morning, give it a like so it

432
00:25:04,290 --> 00:25:07,610
can reach someone who woke up feeling the same way you did,

433
00:25:07,890 --> 00:25:10,390
share it with someone who needs a gentler start,

434
00:25:10,630 --> 00:25:13,690
and subscribe so we can meet here again tomorrow.

435
00:25:14,430 --> 00:25:18,790
And one more thing. Today we thanked God for the gift of a new day.

436
00:25:18,830 --> 00:25:21,630
But there is a reason that gift keeps arriving,

437
00:25:21,910 --> 00:25:23,350
and it is not because we earned it.

438
00:25:23,390 --> 00:25:28,550
It is his mercy and his grace, and once you begin to understand

439
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:32,230
how deep that goes, thanksgiving changes completely.

440
00:25:32,710 --> 00:25:35,950
That is exactly where we are going next in our prayer for God's

441
00:25:35,990 --> 00:25:40,090
mercy, grace and blessings, and it is waiting for you right now.

442
00:25:40,150 --> 00:25:45,110
Go there when you are ready, and start your day in his presence. God bless you.
